  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIn the steps of a [seek](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#dom-media-seek), it defines that 5-13 are run in parallel. This implies that step 11:\n\n> 11. Set the [current playback position](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#current-playback-position) to the new playback position.\n\nwill not be observable until some point closer to when the playback is able to resume at the new playback position.\n\nHowever, Chrome, Firefox and Safari all appear to synchronously set the official playback position to the new playback position, probably also quantized to whatever internal representation they use in their media pipelines.\n\nThis is especially observable in Firefox, where calling `fastSeek(time)` will result in `currentPosition` returning `time`. Once the seek completes, `currentPosition` becomes the time of the keyframe that was chosen.",
